// Radiation on asteroid belt levels (M4 Belt Up; docs/milestone-4-plan.md §3.8 "Radiation").
// Schema: `ls_sim::radiation::RadiationSettings`. Rates in hull per second, distances in u.
// The dose rate follows the signed distance d to the shelter (the belt volume or the cocoon
// around the exit): 0 deeper than `deep` inside, rising linearly to `surface_rate` at the
// surface, then `slope` more per u outside up to `knee` u, `far_slope` more per u beyond it,
// capped at `cap` (13 u out). It is hull loss that bypasses shields and gadgets and credits
// nobody; a mode scales it (`radiation_scale`). Changing a number changes the data hash.
// Tuned by the Belt Up time trials (M4 C5, ls-bots tests/race_match.rs): skimming 4 u above
// the belt costs a Tinker about one hull per lap (1.6 hp/s); the open line 6 u or more off the
// belt several deaths (2.8 hp/s and up), so it is slower than the belt line; the dive to the
// exit about 20 hp at full boost, less than the 30 % hull a racer respawns with at its gate.
RadiationSettings(
    deep: 4.0,
    surface_rate: 0.8,
    slope: 0.2,
    knee: 4.0,
    far_slope: 0.6,
    cap: 7.0,
)
